M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-235_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"eff19c3d-071a-47b5-bae6-8b48a3343a8c","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision (2026-08-16): accept and document the bounded stale-reclaim TOCTOU window. Keep the current advisory-file mechanism; do not add flock or atomic create-and-rename in this ticket. The queue claim remains the correctness boundary, so the residual risk is limited to redundant drain work. Implementation should add a precise code comment documenting that tradeoff and complete the three already-scoped vocabulary/test gaps without changing runtime locking behavior.","timestamp":1786907213171392001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented per the 2026-08-16 operator decision; runtime locking behavior unchanged.\n\n- Item 1 (reclaim TOCTOU): accepted and documented. A comment at the os.unlink in _acquire_advisory_lock states the window (nothing excludes another drainer between the stamped_file_is_stale verdict and the unlink), why the mkdir leg is not exposed to it (its caller already holds the exclusive fcntl leg; a single-file lock has no kernel leg to inherit), the bounded harm (redundant drain work only; the per-ticket optimistic queue claim remains the correctness boundary), the retry-once self-limit, and the two conditions that would justify revisiting (drain work ceasing to be idempotent, or the queue claim ceasing to be the correctness boundary). No flock, no create-and-rename.\n- Item 2 (torn-stamp vocabulary): _describe_drain_lock_holder now distinguishes 'no ownership stamp' / 'unrecognised ownership stamp' / 'incomplete ownership stamp', verbatim the phrases doctor_locks._existence_report renders, and renders them as 'an unknown holder (<phrase>)' mirroring doctor's 'unknown (<phrase>)'. The phrases are duplicated rather than imported because the dependency would run llm -> _commands; a new parametrized test (test_drain_and_doctor_describe_a_holderless_lock_identically) pins the two surfaces to the same wording so drift fails a test instead of confusing an operator.\n- Item 3: two new tests in tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py assert the drain row's 'unrecognised ownership stamp' and 'incomplete ownership stamp' descriptions (plus holder/pid_state None and the young-lock staleness verdict).\n- Item 4: test_stamp_write_failure_keeps_a_ceiling_bounded_lock forces os.write to raise for the drain lock's fd only, and asserts the fd is still returned, the unattributable-lock WARNING fires, nothing was stamped, and the lock is honoured while young but reclaimed once past the shared wall-clock ceiling.\n\nTDD: the four vocabulary assertions were RED before the change; the item-3/item-4 tests passed on first run, as expected for pure coverage gaps on branches that already existed. make lint and make typecheck green (complexity ratchet: active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0). Gerrit change 1918.\n\nDiscovered work filed and linked: moist-short-lionfish (958e-f4b3) - the enrich drain gate check is O(ticket count) and blows its 20 ms budget on every write.","timestamp":1787175416854411001}],"created_at":1786602104431431001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"57a484d3-bfd9-4849-b0ce-f1f538b0239e","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"aadc-9af6-0e67-4e2a"},{"link_uuid":"13bb1549-7e68-44dd-ac8a-9df2237d99b5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2cac-66d0-0741-416d"},{"link_uuid":"940dc0e8-ca2e-4c2b-a6e7-06a4db99f3df","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"96f4-05f7-2223-405e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nGerrit 1704 (bug knavish-stimulated-bluebottle, merged as f8e6a2507f) gave the enrichment\ndrain lock an owner stamp and a bounded stale-reclaim. The LLM code review passed it +1 but\nraised four ADVISORY findings on the new code. They are non-blocking and were deliberately\nnot folded into that change, but three are cheap quality gaps in code that shipped and one\nneeds a design decision, so they should not simply evaporate.\n\n## Approach\nTake the three cheap ones directly; decide the first one explicitly rather than by default.\n\n1. **Reclaim TOCTOU (needs a decision, `enrich_drain._acquire_advisory_lock`).** There is no\n   exclusion between `stamped_file_is_stale` and the `os.unlink`, unlike the mkdir leg, which\n   is safe only because its caller already holds the fcntl leg. Two drainers can both condemn\n   the same orphan and the loser's unlink can remove the winner's fresh lock, so mutual\n   exclusion is defeasible and two drains can run at once. Harm is bounded — the lock only\n   prevents redundant WORK and the queue claim is separately optimistic and lease-bounded —\n   so this is not a correctness hazard, and it is strictly better than the permanent wedge it\n   replaced. Closing it properly means giving the drain lock a kernel leg (`flock`) or an\n   atomic create-and-rename, i.e. changing the locking MECHANISM. Decide: accept and document\n   the window, or adopt a mechanism. Do NOT leave it undocumented.\n2. **Torn-stamp vocabulary (`_describe_drain_lock_holder`).** It collapses an incomplete v2\n   stamp into \"an unstamped drain lock\", while doctor's `_existence_report` distinguishes\n   \"unknown (incomplete ownership stamp)\". Two surfaces describing one artifact should agree.\n3. **Untested doctor branches (`doctor_locks._existence_report`).** The drain row's\n   \"unrecognised ownership stamp\" and \"incomplete ownership stamp\" descriptions have no test.\n4. **Untested stamp-write failure (`_acquire_advisory_lock`).** The branch where `os.write`\n   raises, logs the unattributable-lock WARNING, and still returns the fd is untested; its\n   contract is that the lock stays ceiling-bounded.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py` — item 1's outcome (comment or mechanism) and item 2.\n- `tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py` — item 4.\n- `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py` — item 3.\n\n## Testing\nA test forcing `os.write` to raise asserts acquisition still succeeds, the WARNING fires, and\nthe resulting unstamped lock is still reclaimable once past the ceiling. Two doctor tests\nplant a non-v2 stamp and a truncated v2 stamp and assert each `holder_description`. If item 1\nadopts a mechanism, a concurrency test drives two acquirers across the reclaim window.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The reclaim window is resolved explicitly: either a code comment states the window and\n      why it is acceptable, or a mechanism removes it — verified by reading the diff.\n      DONE per the 2026-08-16 operator decision (accept and document; no flock, no atomic\n      create-and-rename). The merged diff adds the comment at the `os.unlink` site stating the\n      window, the bounded harm, and why the fix is deferred — \"The window is left open\n      deliberately: ... reclaim converges rather than spinning.\" Runtime locking behaviour\n      unchanged, as the decision required.\n- [x] `_describe_drain_lock_holder` distinguishes an incomplete v2 stamp from an unstamped\n      lock, using the same wording as doctor — asserted by a test on a truncated stamp.\n      DONE — `test_torn_stamp_is_described_as_incomplete_not_unstamped` plus\n      `test_drain_and_doctor_describe_a_holderless_lock_identically` for the shared wording.\n- [x] The drain row's \"unrecognised ownership stamp\" description is asserted by a test.\n      DONE — `test_an_unrecognised_drain_stamp_is_stated_not_guessed`.\n- [x] The drain row's \"incomplete ownership stamp\" description is asserted by a test.\n      DONE — `test_an_incomplete_drain_stamp_is_stated_not_guessed`.\n- [x] The stamp-write-failure branch is covered by a test asserting the fd is still returned\n      and the WARNING is logged.\n      DONE — `test_stamp_write_failure_keeps_a_ceiling_bounded_lock`.\n- [x] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and CI's pytest invocation are green.\n      DONE — Gerrit change 1918 earned LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 and MERGED to main as\n      9bfe4b428a. CI green is what the Verified +1 certifies.\n\n## Landing record\nGerrit 1918 merged as 9bfe4b428a, touching src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py (+56),\ntests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py (+90), tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py (+34) —\n177 insertions across exactly the three files in the declared file_impact.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py","reason":"Document the accepted bounded reclaim race and align incomplete-stamp wording without changing the locking mechanism."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py","reason":"Cover incomplete-stamp wording and stamp-write-failure behavior."},{"path":"tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py","reason":"Cover unrecognised and incomplete ownership-stamp descriptions."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2cac-66d0-0741-416d"],["relates_to","96f4-05f7-2223-405e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b69b2dac-fa28-42fc-b8a8-1fd31501e99e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8d78-ef59-83cd-4d76","ticket_type":"task","title":"Close out the drain-lock code-review advisories","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e2858575-5de5-4de4-b060-72f5db62a60e","c00d1a31-a869-4f72-98aa-dd7edf62a48d","b5ea2998-0970-4d50-888b-4e7400001bd4","985bc713-91f8-49d2-9eaf-f8222b50fbf0","34f23d14-3a61-41c8-b81e-b7f4dfd04907","c3ff8cee-08c4-449f-874e-1f97292a6709","13bb1549-7e68-44dd-ac8a-9df2237d99b5","940dc0e8-ca2e-4c2b-a6e7-06a4db99f3df","2895499f-1f58-4d42-8f6d-b9ac7b91dae1","d1c9cd37-30e8-4f28-8415-2134effe0259","b69b2dac-fa28-42fc-b8a8-1fd31501e99e","5cc041ec-680a-40f0-ba34-c993d8a1dc13"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787180454860305001,"uuid":"36da5eb5-af91-4a5b-9c0d-ca52e5d314b9"}